# Model-type-scoped EventDisp for NetworkPath. Alarm rules in EventDisp are scoped to the
# model type that receives the event -- AppNetaAdmin/EventDisp's A/C directives never fire for
# an event that Field 9 routes onto a NetworkPath model, even though the event itself lands
# there correctly. Broadcom docs: "To raise an alarm on several different model types, you must
# create separate event map entries in each model type-specific EventDisp file."
#
# Only the families whose itemType is NETWORK_PATH, plus Unknown (the rule-name fallback, which
# can carry either itemType) -- MultipleWebErrors/WebErrors are WEB_PATH-only and belong in
# WebPath.EventDisp instead. Event-tier codes are declared bare (no action) for the same reason
# as the AppNetaAdmin copy: alarm_bridge already decided in Python that this severity doesn't
# warrant a real alarm.

0x6732150 E 20 A { v 322 SDN_INTEG.IntelligentAlarmSeverity }, 0x6732150, 301
0x6732151 E 20 C 0x6732150, 301
